Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 01:56:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 033/154] refactor: the command intercepts are a decision, not
 a wall of ifs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WillExecuteCommand and ExecuteCommand each held a chain of conditions with no
test over any of them. The policy is now atrium_command_intercept_decision.h -
values in, an answer out, no AppKit and no Browser - and the two methods gather
inputs and switch.

Fifteen tests, one per intercepted command plus the gates that turn each one
off. Three of them cover the crash guards, which are the reason this list
matters: the stock handlers do not degrade on a chromeless window, they die.
Split view NOTREACHEDs with no BrowserView-backed TabCollection, the find bar
dereferences a null owner, and chrome://newtab has no footer controller. A
command quietly dropped from this list does not fail a test, it crashes a
window.

Half the gates read the dylib and go false at the cut. Written as inputs, the
policy survives H2 unchanged and only the callers change - which is why this
is worth doing before the cut rather than after.

COMPILED, NOT EXERCISED. This is live keyboard dispatch and the scenario suite
is busy with a baseline; the VM check has not run.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
